Model files (not stored in this repository)
-------------------------------------------
The Raspberry Pi runtime needs model files that git does not track. They are
not covered by the statement above, except where noted.

1. Pose model: Ultralytics YOLO26n-pose, exported to NCNN (fp32, 320 x 320).
   Licence: AGPL-3.0 (https://www.ultralytics.com/license). Reproduce it from
   the Ultralytics release (the deployed export was made with ultralytics 8.4.37):
       yolo export model=yolo26n-pose.pt format=ncnn imgsz=320
   Commercial use without releasing source requires an Ultralytics Enterprise
   License.

2. Fall models: lpn13_fp32.tflite, event_tcn_v2_fp32.tflite and
   edge/head_point_v2/head_point_v2.json were trained or calibrated on the
   NTU RGB+D dataset. NTU RGB+D may be used for non-commercial research only,
   and redistribution or derivation requires permission from the ROSE Lab
   (https://rose1.ntu.edu.sg/dataset/actionRecognition/). These files, and the
   reference fall times and other data derived from NTU RGB+D, are therefore not
   distributed. The training code in training/ (AGPL-3.0, see training/README.md)
   lets users who hold an NTU RGB+D licence regenerate them.

The hardware-free example (README, "Try the workflow without a Raspberry Pi")
uses generated scores and keypoints and needs none of these files; without the
calibrated head-point table it uses a neutral one.

Third-party data file
---------------------
edge/camera_tuning/imx519_af.json is a camera tuning file in the Raspberry Pi
libcamera format for the Arducam IMX519 module, adapted from the tuning file
that Arducam distributes with its libcamera packages. It is used only when the
device runs that sensor; it carries the terms of its source, not AGPL-3.0.

